    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W3867" name="W3867. Returns &amp; Refund Abuse Prevention" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Return/refund event (links to VS-32.1); refund request
Frequency: Continuous (~0.04% return rate on 2.8M monthly POS txns — the ~40/day AR-credit-memo returns canon — plus ecommerce returns)
Volume: ~14,500 returns/yr (the AR-credit-memo canon); ~1–3% flagged as abuse
Owner: Fraud Management / Returns
Participants: Fraud Management, Returns/Customer Service (links to VS-32.1/VS-09), Store Ops (links to VS-07), Ecommerce (links to VS-10), Payments (links to VS-80), Loyalty (links to VS-13), LP (links to VS-23)
Source: workflow W3867 — Returns &amp; Refund Abuse Prevention</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3867_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3867_Lane1" name="Fraud Management">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3867_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3867_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3867_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3867_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3867_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3867_Start3" name="Return/refund event (links to VS-32.1); refund request">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3867_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3867_Task4" name="Fraud Management/Returns score returns for abuse patterns…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Fraud Management/Returns score returns for abuse patterns: return-without-receipt, wardrobbing/return-after-use, receipt-reuse/duplicate-receipt, refund-to-different-tender, empty-box/switch, stolen-then-returned, receipt-fraud via fake invoices, and returns to abuse promo/loyalty (links to VS-32.1)
Responsible (R): Fraud Management / Returns / LP
Accountable (A): Fraud Management Lead
Duration: Per return</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3867_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3867_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3867_Task5" name="Fraud Management apply controls: refund authorization thresholds, store credit…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Fraud Management apply controls: refund authorization thresholds, store credit vs cash for flagged returns, blacklist/return-ban for serial abusers (links to VS-126), and restock-damage recovery (links to VS-90 damage claims)
Responsible (R): Fraud Management / Returns / Store Ops
Accountable (A): Fraud Management Lead
Duration: Per case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3867_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3867_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3867_Task6" name="Fraud Management/Payments reconcile refund-to-card and original-tender matching…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Fraud Management/Payments reconcile refund-to-card and original-tender matching (links to VS-80), detect refund-fraud rings across stores, and feed cases (links to W3860)
Responsible (R): Fraud Management / Payments
Accountable (A): Fraud Management Lead
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3867_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3867_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3867_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3867_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3867_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-605 (ensure controlled execution — Channel-Specific Fraud Prevention &amp; Detection (PA-125.2).) | - operational: tender-match and store-credit routing; operational: targeted scoring and policy transparency
Owner: Fraud Management / Returns</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
