    <bpmn:process id="W_W3868" name="W3868. Promotion, Coupon &amp; Loyalty Abuse Prevention" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Coupon/promo redemption (links to VS-58); loyalty earn/burn
Frequency: Continuous (peak during bi-monthly sales and double-points weekends)
Volume: Millions of promo/coupon/loyalty events/yr; ~0.5–2% flagged
Owner: Fraud Management / Marketing / Loyalty
Participants: Fraud Management, Marketing (links to VS-14/VS-58), Loyalty (links to VS-13), Ecommerce (links to VS-10), POS (links to VS-08), Merchandising (links to VS-01.2), Insights (links to VS-28.1)
Source: workflow W3868 — Promotion, Coupon &amp; Loyalty Abuse Prevention</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3868_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3868_Lane1" name="Fraud Management">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3868_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3868_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3868_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3868_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3868_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3868_Start3" name="Coupon/promo redemption (links to VS-58); loyalty earn/burn">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3868_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3868_Task4" name="Fraud Management/Marketing/Loyalty prevent coupon/promo abuse…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Fraud Management/Marketing/Loyalty prevent coupon/promo abuse: stacking-discount violations (links to VS-58), expired/fake/photocopied coupons, code-leak and bulk-redemption on digital promos (links to VS-58), price-override-to-promo abuse, and ineligible-SKU promo application (links to VS-01.2)
Responsible (R): Fraud Management / Marketing / Loyalty
Accountable (A): Fraud Management Lead
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
