    <bpmn:process id="W_W3872" name="W3872. Trade / B2B Account &amp; Application First-Party Fraud Prevention" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Trade/B2B account application (links to VS-16/VS-11); order on credit
Frequency: ~5,200 trade accounts + ~200 corporate; ~3,500 AR invoices/month
Volume: Account-application fraud ~1–3% of new trade applications
Owner: Fraud Management / Trade Credit
Participants: Fraud Management, Trade Credit (links to VS-16/VS-68), Trade Sales (links to VS-11/VS-107), Key Account (links to VS-107), KYC/AML (links to VS-86), AR (links to VS-16), Legal (links to VS-100)
Source: workflow W3872 — Trade / B2B Account &amp; Application First-Party Fraud Prevention</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3872_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3872_Lane1" name="Fraud Management">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3872_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3872_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3872_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3872_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3872_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3872_Start3" name="Trade/B2B account application (links to VS-16/VS-11); order on credit">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3872_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3872_Task4" name="Fraud Management/Trade-Credit screen new trade/B2B applications for…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Fraud Management/Trade-Credit screen new trade/B2B applications for first-party/application fraud: identity/business misrepresentation (fake/fraudulent business — verify with SEC/DTI/BIR), synthetic identity, related-party to existing bad-debt accounts (links to VS-126 identity graph), and credit-history gaps
Responsible (R): Fraud Management / Trade Credit / KYC
Accountable (A): Fraud Management Lead
Duration: Per application</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3872_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3872_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3872_Task5" name="Fraud Management/AML run KYB/KYC and sanctions screening on trade accounts…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Fraud Management/AML run KYB/KYC and sanctions screening on trade accounts (links to VS-86), verify trade references and bank details (with PADME/court check), and set credit limit commensurate with verified risk (links to VS-16/VS-68)
Responsible (R): Fraud Management / KYC / Trade Credit
Accountable (A): Fraud Management Lead
Duration: Per application</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3872_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3872_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3872_Task6" name="Fraud Management/AR monitor in-life trade-account fraud: sudden over-ordering…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Fraud Management/AR monitor in-life trade-account fraud: sudden over-ordering, payment-diversion/bank-detail-change fraud (BEC), Bust-out (max credit then disappear), and inflated-revenue-for-bid-bond fraud (links to VS-116) — coordinate recovery (links to VS-16/VS-68/W3874)
Responsible (R): Fraud Management / AR / Trade Sales
Accountable (A): Fraud Management Lead
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3872_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3872_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3872_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3872_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3872_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-605 (ensure controlled execution — Channel-Specific Fraud Prevention &amp; Detection (PA-125.2).) | - operational: SEC/DTI/BIR verification and KYB; operational: callback-verification control (links to VS-18/VS-86)
Owner: Fraud Management / Trade Credit</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W3872_Assoc9" sourceRef="W3872_Annotation8" targetRef="W3872_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
